### Sample 03 — multiple destinations
### The API runs on 5113; the two receivers on 5111 and 5112.

@api = http://localhost:5113
@receiverA = http://localhost:5111
@receiverB = http://localhost:5112

### The sample's index — what this app exposes
GET {{api}}/

### The registered destinations and the transport serving each one
GET {{api}}/destinations

### Place an order. One event, three destinations, three outbox ids.
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "customerId": "cust-1",
  "total": 99.50
}

### What receiver A got
GET {{receiverA}}/deliveries

### What receiver B got
GET {{receiverB}}/deliveries

### Counts only, if the full bodies are noisy
GET {{receiverA}}/deliveries/summary

###
GET {{receiverB}}/deliveries/summary

### The third destination writes files instead — look in 03-MultipleDestinations/audit.

### Clear both receivers between experiments
DELETE {{receiverA}}/deliveries

###
DELETE {{receiverB}}/deliveries
